--
-- Changes applied, and why (the real production schema has constraints
-- Session 7-T's own minimal disposable-Postgres schema did not enforce):
--   1. dataset_id = 'CMA_POC_500_V1' added to every row in
--      customer_interactions, chat_sessions, qa_reviews, automated_qa_evaluations
--      (qa_findings/automated_qa_observations get no column of their own --
--      always filtered via their join to a tagged parent).
--   2. agent_id remapped from the 5 synthetic cma500_agent_1..5 values to
--      exactly two new values, VF_TEST_AGENT_A / VF_TEST_AGENT_B (internal
--      synthetic POC identities only -- no agents table exists in this
--      schema, no external VoiceForce Conversational Agent identity is
--      created, no real call/message is ever triggered). Mapping:
--        cma500_agent_2, cma500_agent_3, cma500_agent_4 -> VF_TEST_AGENT_A (262 rows)
--        cma500_agent_1, cma500_agent_5                 -> VF_TEST_AGENT_B (228 rows)
--      Rows with a null agent_id (~10, a deliberate "missing agent" test
--      scenario) are left null, never force-assigned.
--   3. customer_interactions.customer_id and .campaign_id, and
--      chat_sessions.campaign_id, are set to null -- the synthetic customer/
--      campaign ids Session 7-T's minimal schema didn't FK-check do not
--      exist as real rows in production's customers/campaigns tables, and
--      inserting fake rows there would itself contaminate Customer 360's
--      and the Campaigns screen's completely unfiltered list views (a
--      documented Session 7.1 scope decision -- see
--      docs/SESSION_7_1_CMA_TEST_DATA_UI_VALIDATION.md). Nulling these is
--      also semantically correct, not just a workaround: CMA's own sync
--      path already legitimately writes null customer_id for rows with no
--      identity resolution (see cmaSyncMapping.ts), and no CMA measure
--      tested here reads customer_id/campaign_id at all.
--   4. customer_interactions.source changed from 'cma500-synthetic' to the
--      real, check-constraint-allowed 'call-data' value (source in
--      ('call-data','chat-sessions') is enforced in production; Session
--      7-T's minimal schema did not have this constraint).
--   5. qa_reviews.reviewer_user_id and automated_qa_evaluations.initiated_by
--      (both NOT NULL + FK to user_profiles(id) in production; the first
--      was null and the second was entirely absent in Session 7-T's
--      fixtures, neither of which production's real constraints allow) are
--      set to a real, existing user_profiles row
--      (d7f1a4ce-de44-4e7e-8610-f5f38ebf3db7, shripad@tardis.solutions --
--      the account authorizing this population), rather than fabricating a
--      new user_profiles row, which would itself appear unconditionally
--      (no dataset filter exists) in the User Management screen.
--
-- Row counts: 350 customer_interactions, 150 chat_sessions, 80 qa_reviews
